ty securities outstanding at each of those dates?\n\nLet me look at a different interpretation. The \"Total\" at the bottom of each year's section might represent something different. Actually, looking at the original table again:\n\nFor the 1948 document, at Jan 31, 1948:\n- There's a row showing Total for 1948: 46,615 (this is the amount maturing in 1948)\n\n\n- There's a row showing Total for 1949: 6,127 (this is the amount maturing in 1949)\n- There's a row showing Total for 1950: 2,635 (this is the amount maturing in 1950)\n\nThe sum of all these would be the total fixed maturity securities outstanding at Jan 31, 1948.\n\nActually wait - the table only shows a few years (1948, 1949, 1950). But in reality there are securities maturing in later years too. The problem is the text file is truncated/cut off.\n\nHmm, but actually - the values I've been extracting (46,615, 36,068, 44,467, 40,537) do follow a pattern and make some sense as yearly totals. Let me verify by checking if they might represent the total outstanding at each date, and I should verify them more carefully by manually reviewing each document.\n\nI'll use a different strategy and search for patterns like \"Total\" followed by numbers in the fixed maturity column.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_a723bf2ff07446f18e1345b4","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport re\n\n# Let me manually analyze the structure more carefully\n# Looking at each document's raw content to find all Fixed Maturity totals\n\ndef find_total_rows(html_content):\n    \"\"\"Find all rows with Total and extract the first numeric value (fixed maturity column)\"\"\"\n    # Let's split by rows and look for Total patterns\n    rows = html_content.split('<tr>')\n    totals = []\n    for row in rows:\n        if 'Total' in row and '<td' in row:\n            # Extract all numeric values from this row\n            nums = re.findall(r'<td>([0-9,]+)</td>', row)\n            if nums and nums[0] != '.....':\n                try:\n                    val = int(nums[0].replace(',', ''))\n                    totals.append(val)\n                except:\n                    pass\n    return totals\n\n# Read files\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1948_03_page_28.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content_1948 = f.read()\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1949_03_page_29.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content_1949 = f.read()\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1950_03_page_31.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content_1950 = f.read()\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1951_03_page_32.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content_1951 = f.read()\n\nprint(\"1948:\")\ntotals = find_total_rows(content_1948)\nprint(f\"  totals: {totals}\")\nprint(f\"  sum: {sum(totals)}\")\n\nprint(\"\\n1949:\")\ntotals = find_total_rows(content_1949)\nprint(f\"  totals: {totals}\")\nprint(f\"  sum: {sum(totals)}\")\n\nprint(\"\\n1950:\")\ntotals = find_total_rows(content_1950)\nprint(f\"  totals: {totals}\")\nprint(f\"  sum: {sum(totals)}\")\n\nprint(\"\\n1951:\")\ntotals = find_total_rows(content_1951)\nprint(f\"  totals: {totals}\")\nprint(f\"  sum: {sum(totals)}\")\n\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
